Step 1: Create a Notification Component

Create a new file:

src/components/Notification.jsx
const Notification = ({ message }) => {
  if (message === null) {
    return null;
  }

  return (
    <div className="success">
      {message}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Notification;

If message is null, nothing is rendered.

Step 2: Add CSS

In your index.css (or App.css), add:

.success {
  color: green;
  background: lightgrey;
  font-size: 20px;
  border: 2px solid green;
  border-radius: 5px;
  padding: 10px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

This matches the green success notification shown in the exercise.

Step 3: Add Notification State

In App.jsx:

import Notification from "./components/Notification";

Create a new piece of state:

const [message, setMessage] = useState(null);
Step 4: Render the Notification

Near the top of your component:

<h2>Phonebook</h2>

<Notification message={message} />

Whenever message is not null, the notification will appear.

Step 5: Show a Message When Adding a Person

Inside your create request:

personService.create(personObject).then(returnedPerson => {
  setPersons(persons.concat(returnedPerson));

  setMessage(`Added ${returnedPerson.name}`);

  setTimeout(() => {
    setMessage(null);
  }, 5000);

  setNewName("");
  setNewNumber("");
});

The notification appears immediately and disappears after 5 seconds.

Step 6: Show a Message When Updating a Number

Inside your update request:

personService
  .update(existingPerson.id, updatedPerson)
  .then(returnedPerson => {
    setPersons(
      persons.map(person =>
        person.id !== existingPerson.id
          ? person
          : returnedPerson
      )
    );

    setMessage(`Updated ${returnedPerson.name}`);

    setTimeout(() => {
      setMessage(null);
    }, 5000);

    setNewName("");
    setNewNumber("");
  });
